# 3. CONFIGURATION ARCHITECTURE

Implement a centralized configuration management architecture.

Logical architecture:

Agent Registry  
→ Agent Configuration Definition  
→ Configuration Schema Resolver  
→ Default Configuration Resolver  
→ Agent-Specific Configuration Resolver  
→ Authorized Organization Configuration Resolver  
→ Configuration Validator  
→ Configuration Normalizer  
→ Active Configuration Version Resolver  
→ Resolved Agent Configuration  
→ Agent Execution Engine

The framework must produce a validated, version-specific configuration object before an agent execution begins.

The execution engine must receive a resolved configuration snapshot rather than independently assembling configuration from multiple database sources.

The actual implementation must follow the existing GeFlow technology stack and architecture.

