# 10. CONFIGURATION LIFECYCLE

Implement a controlled configuration lifecycle.

Recommended statuses:

| Status | Meaning |
|---|---|
| draft | Configuration is being created or edited |
| validating | Configuration is undergoing validation |
| validated | Configuration passed validation |
| approved | Configuration received required approval |
| active | Configuration is currently approved for standard execution |
| superseded | A newer configuration replaced it |
| deprecated | Configuration should no longer be used |
| archived | Configuration is retained for historical reference |

Requirements:

- Define valid state transitions.
- Enforce authorized transitions.
- Validate before activation.
- Preserve historical configurations.
- Prevent unauthorized activation.
- Prevent normal execution from using draft or deprecated configurations.
- Maintain one active configuration version per agent and applicable scope, according to the existing versioning model.

Do not invent an approval workflow if the existing platform has not defined one. Report any missing governance policy.

